 "headline": "Gate B (concentration-rescues-ignition): MET at the demonstrated pore. At the vent-posterior base feed (1e-03 M, held equal), the concentrating pore (porosity 0.88, enrichment 23x, pore-local feed 2.33e-02 M) IGNITES the network (net_carbon_flux +4.43e-04, connected, 17 persistent species) while the matched well-mixed nonconcentrating control does NOT (flux -1.80e-08, not connected). WINDOW (empirical, not extrapolated): connected-ignition occupies a BOUNDED porosity band (ignited+physical at porosity in [0.9, 0.8]) \u2014 below it enrichment is sub-threshold, above it the pore-local feed becomes physically implausible; net carbon flux is monotone in enrichment while network_connected is brittle near threshold. NOT a broad robust swath. This resolves Gate A's A1 feed-plausibility: a carbon-fixing network persists at vent-realistic feeds in a pore within that geometry window. C6 confirmation: demo pore ignited=True (flux +4.46e-04), control ignited=False, tight pore ignited=False."
